    2                      ;  19_given_all_general -- the provided all-instruction example, made runnable
    3                      ;=============================================================================
    4                      ;  The body between 'l1:' and the final store block is the provided example,
    5                      ;  unchanged.  As provided it could not be checked:
    6                      ;
    7                      ;    - with every register at 0, its fifth instruction, lw r19, 63(r8), reads
    8                      ;      address 63, which is misaligned.  The trap vectors to VBR + 12 = 0x0C,
    9                      ;      which re-executes the andi and the same lw, so the program never got
   10                      ;      past instruction 5;
   11                      ;    - it ended in "j l1", so it never reached a final state;
   12                      ;    - it has no stores, so the final memory image showed nothing.
   13                      ;
   14                      ;  So, around the unchanged body:
   15                      ;    - the prologue gives every register a distinct value.  Four of them are
   16                      ;      chosen so each load is aligned and inside the 2 KB data memory:
   17                      ;        r8  = 1   lw  r19, 63(r8)  -> 0x40
   18                      ;        r2  = 1   lb  r1, -1(r2)   -> 0x00
   19                      ;        r3  = 0   sll r1, r2, r3 = 1, so slli r4 = 32 and lbu r3, 1(r4) -> 0x21
   20                      ;        r12 = 1   xori r6, r12, 1 = 0, so lhu r2, 32(r6) -> 0x20
   21                      ;    - "j l1" is replaced by stores of r1..r31 and the usual final self-loop.
   22                      ;
   23                      ;  Result map: words 64..94 (0x100..0x178) hold r1..r31.
   24                      ;=============================================================================
